  "honest_note": "Absolute anchor cosine EXCEEDS 0.90 (mean-pool deva ~0.99), so the paper's literal >0.90 claim is reproduced -- BUT generic MuRIL embeddings are anisotropic, so mismatched and neutral word pairs also score ~0.99; the absolute number alone is therefore not evidence of semantic alignment. The anisotropy-robust evidence is the positive matched-minus-mismatched/neutral MARGIN + the point-biserial (akela/akelapan r~0.6) + the t-SNE structure. Domain-adaptive fine-tuning is the methodology's remedy to de-anisotropise and widen the margin; reported as-measured (P-series honesty)."
